data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Empty repo. Now I need to write DESIGN.md. The mission requires:\n- A greeting the viewer can change the colour of by clicking a button\n- From `@codesweep-ai/ui`: `Header`, `Footer`, `Button`, colour tokens\n- Header and Footer belong to AppShell (per developer brief)\n- Keep the design small enough to build and check in one pass\n- Name design system components rather than colours and pixels\n\nI should check the catalog to know what's available... but the package isn't installed yet in my clone. The developer will install it. The developer brief says catalog.json is at node_modules/@codesweep-ai/ui/catalog.json. I could install it myself to peek at the catalog to inform the design — but the orchestrator \"does not write the application.\" Installing the package to read the catalog isn't writing the app; but it's probably unnecessary. The mission says: \"The package ships a catalog.json naming everything else it offers.\" and my brief says \"your design says how those fit together and what else it takes from the catalog.\"\n\nI could npm-install the package in a temp dir just to read the catalog so my design names real components. That would make the design grounded. Let me do that quickly — it's a design aid, not app code. Let me check network availability first by just trying.\n\nActually, let me think about what tokens exist. The tokens are `--color-*`. Without reading the package I'd guess token names like `--color-blue-500` etc. Better to actually read the package. Let me install it in /tmp."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793342551,"id":"chatcmpl-9de98f1e","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

